# Messaging views and sessions

See `about.md` § WebContentsView Manager, § Persistent Sessions, § Add Account Flow, § Delete Account Flow, § Performance Strategy.

## MessagingViewManager

Centralized service in the main process with this API:

```
createView(accountId)
showView(accountId)
hideView(accountId)
destroyView(accountId)
reloadView(accountId)
clearSession(accountId)
getView(accountId)
resizeActiveView(bounds)
```

Use `Map<string, WebContentsView>` internally.

## View lifecycle rules

- Only the selected account view should be visible.
- Inactive opened accounts remain alive (hidden) to maintain connection and notifications.
- Do not destroy and recreate views every time the user switches tabs.
- Closing a tab does not log out, delete the account, or delete its session.
- Deleting an account must: destroy view → clear session → remove metadata → close tab → remove from sidebar.

## Partitions

- Format: `persist:mmwa-{platform}-{accountId}` (e.g. `persist:mmwa-whatsapp-a`, `persist:mmwa-telegram-a`).
- Never share one partition between multiple accounts.
- Create partition when account is created; clear on account deletion.

## Platform URLs

- WhatsApp (Personal and Business): `https://web.whatsapp.com/`
- Telegram: official Telegram Web client URL (use a named constant; verify at implementation time).

## Window integration

- Attach views via `BrowserWindow.contentView.addChildView()`.
- Call `resizeActiveView(bounds)` when the content area resizes; bounds come from the shell layout (sidebar + tabs offset).
- Messaging views must not receive the application preload bridge.

## Performance (Phase 1)

- Active account: visible and fully active.
- Inactive opened accounts: alive but hidden.
- Deleted accounts: destroyed.
- Do not enable account suspension by default.
